  "contract": {
    "label_ace": "Require a present non-NULL valid ACL containing exactly one ACE; GetAce index zero must lie wholly within the validated ACL. Require mandatory label ACE type and a bounded one-subauthority valid SID with SECURITY_MANDATORY_LABEL_AUTHORITY. Derived equality checks exact ACE type, ACE inheritance flags, policy mask and all SID bytes including revision/authority/RID. No string trimming, prefix removal or mask relaxation.",
    "acl_control": "AI is an SDDL ACL control token. Original actual label SDDL and numeric descriptor control/revision remain observed; template-vs-object label equality compares the precise label ACE rather than requiring the template to acquire native ACL control bits.",
    "original_custody": "The actual Descriptor allocation captured from the same retained handle is unchanged and kept intact. No descriptor control mutation API is added. Existing survivor restore still applies that original label and requires complete ALL_INFO string equality, now also exact descriptor control/revision equality. Deleted pending objects retain the original close/name-check behavior; they are not resurrected.",
    "label_apply_and_finish": "Both after-set and pre-finish mandatory-label checks use the same strict single-ACE predicate. Owner/group/DACL equality and same-object identity assertions remain exact. Original expected label SDDL remains in observation JSON.",
    "same_object": "No new handles or path opens, no sharing/rights changes, no production flags, no timing changes. All added Windows calls query the existing native descriptor, except existing label setter which remains byte-identical."
  },
